title: Moscow's Letter
subtitle: The Executive has written to the congress.
view-if: congress = 1 and congress_closing = 0 and congress_used_moscow = 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.congress_used_moscow = 1;
RG.congress.tally();
Q.sys_outcome = 0;
!}
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: congress

= Moscow's Letter

A courier from the Executive has brought a letter to the congress, signed by Zinoviev for the Communist International. It is long, it quotes Lenin twice, and it leaves no doubt that Moscow stands with the **[+ moscow_backs_name +]**.

[? if congress_moscow_with_us = 1 : That is our side. ?][? if congress_moscow_with_us = 0 : That is not our side. ?] The delegates know a letter has come. They do not yet know what it says.

- @read: Read the letter to the congress.
- @read_anyway: Read it, as discipline demands.
- @suppress: Keep the letter in the drawer.
- @envoy: Let the envoy speak for the Executive.

@read
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Wins delegates who look to Moscow. Our independence suffers a little.
view-if: congress_moscow_with_us = 1
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
}
RG.congress.sway(0.06 + Math.random() * 0.03);
Q.independence -= 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 3);
!}

The chair reads the letter aloud. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : Delegates who were wavering do not waver any more: [+ congress_last_moved +] of them come over to us. ?] The rest mutter that the German party used to decide its own questions.

@read_anyway
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Some delegates go over to Moscow's side, ours among them. Moscow will be grateful.
view-if: congress_moscow_with_us = 0
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
}
RG.congress.swayTo(Q.moscow_backs, 0.07);
Q.independence -= 4;
RG.ecci('all', 5);
!}

We read the letter in full, because a section of the International does not hide the International's letters from its own congress. The [+ moscow_backs_name +] cheer. [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates go over to them.

@suppress
subtitle: Our independence grows, and Moscow will hear of it. The letter may leak.
view-if: congress_moscow_with_us = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 3;
RG.ecci('all', -6);
if (Math.random() < 0.4) {
    Q.sys_outcome = 2;
    RG.congress.bitter(3);
    RG.congress.swayTo(Q.moscow_backs, 0.04);
} else {
    Q.sys_outcome = 1;
}
!}

The letter stays in the Zentrale's drawer. [? if sys_outcome = 1 : Nobody outside the Zentrale learns what it said. ?][? if sys_outcome = 2 : By the second day, the [+ moscow_backs_name +] are quoting it from the floor. The delegates want to know what else we are hiding. ?]

@envoy
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] [+ comintern_rep +] can move the hall like nobody else. Moscow's man in our congress is a precedent.
view-if: comintern_rep and congress_moscow_with_us = 1
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 5;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
}
RG.congress.sway(0.1);
Q.independence -= 6;
RG.ecci('all', 3);
!}

[+ comintern_rep +] takes the floor and speaks for the whole International. [? if congress_last_moved > 0 : [+ congress_last_moved +] delegates come over to us. ?] Afterwards, some delegates ask who elected him.
